      "created_at": "2026-07-23T03:34:18Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-23T03:34:18Z",
      "body": "Thanks for picking this up — but the canonical definition has already landed and this PR conflicts with it on every file. Current main: bits_per_token is the single canonical field (f64) across the Gate C harness and report schema, with the definition in docs/transformerless/GLOSSARY.md and the historical families annotated in BASELINE.md (issue #76, commit 1615127). The two-field approach here (wb_bits_per_token + an Optional bits_per_token with a fallback) reintroduces exactly the ambiguity #76 resolved by naming the scorer+distribution alongside values instead of splitting the metric. Also note the baseline_kappa.json change — the pin moves only by explicit maintainer re-pin (AGENTS.md documents the procedure). If you'd like to take one of the open chain issues (#69, #71–#75, #77–#80 under tracker #65), several are ready and unassigned; happy to point you at a good first one (#77 CI trend tracking is small and self-contained).",
